      "raw": "<p>Had a game tonight where Explosive Bubbles came out, at its initial 5 HP.&nbsp; &quot;\r\n<style type=\"text/css\">\r\n<!--td {border: 1px solid #ccc;}br {mso-data-placement:same-cell;}--></style>\r\n<span style=\"font-size:110.0%;font-family:calibri,arial,sans,sans-serif;color:#000000;text-align:left;\">At the end of the Environment turn, this card deals 2 Energy Damage to the X non-Environment Targets with the highest HP, where X = the current HP of this card.</span>&quot;&nbsp; The 5 highest targets were:</p><p>* Villain Character</p><p>* 3 heroes</p><p>* Villain target</p><p>One of the heroes had a 2-point retaliation attack.&nbsp;</p><p>We reasoned that we got to choose which order to do damage in, since it wasn&#39;t specified.&nbsp; First we damaged the 5-th highest Villain target.&nbsp; Then we hit the Villain character.&nbsp; Then we hit the hero with the retaliation attck.&nbsp; The retaliation reduced EB to 3 HP.&nbsp; We reasoned that since &quot;the current HP of this card&quot; was 3, and it had damaged 3 targets, that we were done.</p><p>Opinions?</p>",
